# What a tool makes in here. The root .gitignore already covers *_silent.mp4,
# *_cues.txt, *_pops.wav and *_hits.wav; this folder's derived files are named
# for what they carry rather than for what made them, so they are named here.
#
# The three cue files are the whole reason render.sh is one command - flowanim.py
# writes them and biohack_audio.py reads them, so neither is ever typed twice -
# but they are outputs, and an output in history is an output somebody edits.
*_chips.txt
*_dials.txt
*_finale.txt
*_sfx.wav

# /icons/ is the rasteriser's cache, and the leading slash is load-bearing: an
# unanchored `icons/` also matches icon-sources/package/icons/, which is the one
# directory in here that must be carried. It quietly excluded all 2077 svgs., keyed by name, size and colour. glyphs.py
# rebuilds any of it in milliseconds from icon-sources/, which IS carried: it is
# the licence and the 2077 svgs, and a build that needs the network is a build
# that fails on a train.
/icons/

# The bed is carried. It is 8 seconds of authored sound whose parameters are in
# biohack_audio.py, and it is deterministic - but so is base_layer.png, and that
# is carried too, for the same reason: the thing every clip is mixed against
# should not depend on nobody having touched a constant.
!biohack_bed_8s.m4a
*_hacks.txt

# <topic>_head.png - a returned poster whose HEADER has been copied back from
# its own base, pixel for pixel, because the generator painted picture into the
# flat title band. It is one command from (poster, base) and both of those are
# kept, so it is a build product like the labelled pair and not an artefact.
# The archival <topic>_poster.jpeg stays exactly as the generator returned it.
*_head.png
